    "final_text": "The todo app is built and all 89 tests pass (`npm test`). It has no dependencies and uses Node's built-in test runner. I also ran every command by hand in a temp directory and the output and exit codes were as expected.\n\n```\n$ node index.js list\n1. [ ] Buy groceries\n2. [x] Walk the dog\n```\n\n**Files**\n- `todos.js`: reading and writing `todos.json`, plus add, complete, delete and list formatting.\n- `index.js`: parses the command and prints results. Errors go to stderr with exit code 1.\n- `package.json`: `\"test\": \"node --test\"`, requires Node 18 or later.\n- `test/todos.test.js`: unit tests for the functions in `todos.js`.\n- `test/cli.test.js`: runs the real `node index.js` in a fresh temp directory for each test.\n- `README.md`: usage and behavior notes. I also added `todos.json` to `.gitignore` so personal todo data doesn't get committed.\n\n**Edge cases handled**\n- **Missing arguments:** `add` with no text, empty or whitespace-only text, and `complete`/`delete` with no id each give a clear error with the usage line.\n- **Invalid ids:** `abc`, `0`, `-1`, `1.5`, `1e3` and ids that don't exist are rejected, and the file is left unchanged.\n- **Empty list:** if there are no todos, or `todos.json` is missing or blank, `list` prints \"No todos yet.\"\n- **Commands:** no command or an unknown command prints the usage text; `help`, `--help` and `-h` also work.\n- **Corrupt `todos.json`:** invalid JSON or malformed entries give a clean error and the file is never overwritten.\n- **Safe saves:** the app writes to a temp file and then renames it, so a crash mid-save can't damage `todos.json`.\n\nTo check that the tests actually catch bugs, I broke the code on purpose 11 different ways (for example: wrong status marker, errors exiting with code 0, `complete` not saving, extra ids being ignored). The tests failed every time.\n\n**Decisions I made where the spec was open**\n- **Todo ids:** a new id is one more than the highest existing id. This keeps `todos.json` a plain list of todos, exactly as specified. The catch is that if you delete the todo with the highest id, the next todo you add gets that same id. Gaps in the middle of the list are never refilled. Never reusing ids would mean storing a counter in the file too.\n- **Unquoted text:** `add Buy groceries` works the same as `add \"Buy groceries\"`.\n- **Completing a finished todo:** this prints a note and exits 0 rather than failing.\n- **Extra ids:** `complete 1 2` is rejected rather than quietly completing only #1.\n\nNothing is committed yet, because you didn't ask me to commit.",
